    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0269" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg189"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Buck to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tokio,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-03-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 623.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    on the 1st instant of instruction<anchor n="a" xml:id="d158-f1"/> No. 385, of
                    date of January 29 last, respecting the restoration <pb facs="0270" n="190"
                        xml:id="pg190"/> as soon as practicable of the city of Tientsin and its
                    suburbs to Chinese authority, and stating that I may make use of the instruction
                    in ascertaining the views of the Japanese Government in that matter, concerning
                    which you would be pleased to have my report.</p>
                <p>To obtain the views of the Japanese Government, as instructed, on the 3d instant
                    I addressed a note to his excellency, the minister of foreign affairs (copy
                    herewith), and to-day I have received his reply (copy inclosed), stating that
                    the Imperial Government share the views of the United States Government that the
                    abolition of the provisional government at Tientsin at an early date is very
                    desirable, without affecting the question of the presence of foreign detachments
                    for the maintenance of free communication between Peking and the sea, and that
                    his Government will make no objection, in event that all the other powers
                    actually participating agree to it.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. E. Buck</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d158-a1.xml" xpointer="d158-a1"/>
